<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">22 April in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 22 April, from 960 to 1970.</p></header>
<div class="tih-pinned-card"><p class="tih-pinned-label">International day</p><p class="tih-pinned-title">Earth Day</p><p class="tih-pinned-desc">First held in 1970 following the Santa Barbara oil spill, Earth Day mobilises over a billion people each year to take action on environmental protection, climate change, and biodiversity loss.</p></div>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/basil-ii" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/basil-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/960">960 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,066 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Basil II is crowned co-emperor of the Byzantine Empire</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basil-ii">Basil II</a> was crowned co-emperor in the reign of his father, Romanos II, but was still too young to rule when Romanos died in 963. He became senior emperor in 976 and reigned until 1025, longer than any other Roman emperor.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1073">1073 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">953 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hildebrand of Sovana is elected Pope Gregory VII</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-gregory-vii">Hildebrand of Sovana</a> was elected pope as Gregory VII, succeeding Pope <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-ii-of-russia">Alexander II</a>. He gave his name to the Gregorian reform, and his struggle with Emperor Henry IV over the investiture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> led to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-henry-the-navigator">Henry</a>'s penance at Canossa in 1077.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-gregory-vii">Pope Gregory VII</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1500">1500 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">526 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pedro Álvares Cabral reaches the coast of Brazil</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A Portuguese fleet bound for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> sighted land in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a> and claimed it for Portugal. The landfall began Portuguese colonisation of what became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, long inhabited by Indigenous peoples.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-alvares-cabral">Pedro Álvares Cabral</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1519">1519 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">507 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hernán Cortés lands at Veracruz</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Cortés landed on the Gulf coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> and soon founded Villa Rica de la Vera Cruz. The settlement served as his base for the conquest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hernan-cortes">Hernán Cortés</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1529">1529 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">497 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles V and John III of Portugal sign the Treaty of Zaragoza</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-king-of-england">King John</a> III of Portugal signed a treaty at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaragoza">Zaragoza</a> dividing Castilian and Portuguese influence in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a> along a line 297.5 leagues east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maluku-islands">Moluccas</a>. Both had claimed these Spice Islands under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-tordesillas">Treaty of Tordesillas</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maluku-islands">Maluku Islands</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1864">1864 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">162 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Coinage Act puts 'In God We Trust' on US coins</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Congress authorised a new two-cent coin, the first to bear the motto 'In God We Trust'. It spread to other coins and became the official US national motto in 1956.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1915">1915 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">111 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Germany releases chlorine gas at Ypres</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">German troops released chlorine from cylinders against French and Algerian positions near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ypres">Ypres</a>. It was the first large-scale use of lethal gas on the Western Front and opened a chemical arms race.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1970">1970 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">56 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Millions mark the first Earth Day</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Some 20 million Americans joined rallies and teach-ins for the first Earth Day. Its momentum helped create the Environmental Protection Agency later that year.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 22 April <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-fielding"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-fielding.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Henry Fielding</span><span class="tp">1707–1754</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/immanuel-kant"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/immanuel-kant.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Immanuel Kant</span><span class="tp">1724–1804</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/charles-denis-bourbaki"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/charles-denis-bourbaki.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Charles-Denis Bourbaki</span><span class="tp">1816–1897</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/william-iv-grand-duke-of-luxembourg"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/william-iv-grand-duke-of-luxembourg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">William IV, Grand Duke of Luxembourg</span><span class="tp">1852–1912</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/vladimir-lenin"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/vladimir-lenin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Vladimir Lenin</span><span class="tp">1870–1924</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 22 April <span class="n">3</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/miguel-de-cervantes"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/miguel-de-cervantes.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Miguel de Cervantes</span><span class="tp">1547–1616</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/james-hargreaves"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">James Hargreaves</span><span class="tp">c. 1720–1778</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/richard-nixon"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/richard-nixon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Richard Nixon</span><span class="tp">1913–1994</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
